course: dictionary
lesson: 9163
title: Snowdrop: the first flower of spring
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A snowdrop is a small plant with a white flower that hangs down like a drop. The name helps you picture it: snow is the white, cold stuff that falls from the sky, and drop is a small round bit of something falling.
explain: Snowdrops are among the first flowers to bloom at the end of winter, sometimes while snow is still on the ground. «Daffodils and snowdrops flower before the trees have leaves», so they bloom while the light still reaches the ground.
explain: Snowdrops grow from bulbs under the soil. A bulb is a store of food. The plant uses that food to flower early, catching sunlight before the trees above it shade the ground.
fact: «Snowdrop» means a small plant with a white flower that hangs down, and that blooms at the end of winter.
fact: Each snowdrop flower has three outer white petals and a small inner cup with green marks.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, snowdrops flower from January to March, a sign that spring is coming.
fact: In stories and poems, snowdrops stand for hope and new beginnings.
fact: Snowdrop bulbs are poisonous if eaten, so never eat any part of a snowdrop.
exercise: What is a snowdrop? | *A small plant with a white flower that hangs down like a drop | A tall tree with green leaves all year round | A kind of snow that falls in summer
exercise: In the UK and Ireland, when do snowdrops usually flower? | *January to March | July to September | December to June | October to November
exercise: In poems and stories, what do snowdrops often stand for? | Speed and noise | Anger and fear | Hunger and thirst | *Hope and new beginnings
test: Which part of a snowdrop is poisonous if eaten? | Its green leaves | The green marks inside the flower | *Its bulb | Its white petals
test: Why is the snowdrop one of the first flowers of the year? | *It blooms at the end of winter, sometimes while snow is still on the ground | It grows only in deep water | It only blooms in the middle of summer | It flowers after all the trees have dropped their leaves in autumn
exam: How many outer white petals does a snowdrop flower have? | Two | Eight | *Three | Five
